3.4 Behavioural Differences

The strongest differences were observed in purchasing and engagement behaviour.

Behavioural Metric	Retained	Churned
Total transactions	56.72	19.57
Total spend	1,837.04	625.24
Average basket value	28.96	24.73
Average app sessions	2.12	1.07
Average emails opened	1.04	0.67
Total coupons redeemed	7.37	3.25
Average distinct categories	2.48	1.81
Total support tickets	1.59	1.89
Complaint rate	4.49%	7.64%

Churned customers show substantially lower purchasing activity and digital engagement than retained customers. They have fewer transactions, lower total spending, fewer app sessions, fewer email opens, fewer coupon redemptions and lower category diversity. Churned customers also show somewhat higher support activity and complaint rates.

3.5 Correlation Analysis

The strongest Spearman associations with the churn label were:

Feature	Spearman Correlation
Total transactions	-0.468
Total spend	-0.457
Average app sessions	-0.433
Total coupons redeemed	-0.425
Average distinct categories	-0.360
Average emails opened	-0.266
Average basket value	-0.243
Total support tickets	+0.100
Complaint rate	+0.103

Higher purchasing and engagement measures are negatively associated with the churn label, while support and complaint measures show small positive associations. These correlations describe relationships in the observed data and do not establish causality.

3.6 Signup Cohort Analysis
Signup Year	Customers	Observed Churn Rate
2021	745	37.45%
2022	792	38.64%
2023	816	28.06%
2024	247	1.62%

The 2021 and 2022 cohorts have higher observed churn rates than the 2023 cohort. The 2024 cohort has a substantially lower observed churn rate; however, this cohort has much shorter observation history and a substantially higher proportion of insufficient-history customers. Therefore, the 2024 result should not be directly interpreted as evidence of lower inherent churn propensity.

